  "question": {
    "text": "The numbers&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></msup></math> form first three terms of an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math>,&nbsp;then its fifth term is"
  },
